
E A
C FOCAL15 V9A
01.01 T !"THIS FOCAL PROGRAM TEACHES FOCAL PROGRAMING.
01.02 T !"A PROGRAM CONSISTS OF COMMANDS TO THE COMPUTER.
01.03 T !"LET'S START BY SEEING HOW TO GET AROUND IN THE
01.04 T !"PROGRAM. TO MAKE THINGS HAPPEN, USE THE RETURN KEY .
01.05 A AN," THE INSTRUCTION GO OR G (EITHER WILL WORK)
01.06 T !,"WILL START THE PROGRAM AT A GIVEN NUMBERED
01.07 T !"LOCATION.  IF NO NUMBER IS GIVEN, EXECUTION
01.08 T !"STARTS AT THE LOWEST NUMBERED LOCATION IN THE ENTIRE PROGRAM.
01.09 T !"TO INTERUPT AT ANY TIME, WHILE DEPRESSING THE
01.10 T !"KEY CONTROL (CTRL) , HIT P. I WILL MAKE IT INTERUPT BY ITSELF
01.11 T !"SO THAT YOU CAN TRY GOING BACK TO AN EARLIER COMMAND. TYPE
01.12 T !" G 1.08 BUT OBSERVE  SPACING. NEXT SEE YOUR GUIDE SHEET"; Q
01.13 T !"EVERY LINE (STATEMENT) HAS A NUMBER.  THE LINES ARE
01.14 T !"IN GROUPS DESIGNATED BY THE FIRST DIGITS. EG. 1.12,1.58,
01.15 T !"1.99 ARE ALL IN GROUP 1. THERE ARE 15 GROUPS.
01.16 T !"YOU WON'T FIND MUCH ABOVE 1.50 BECAUSE THE PROGRAM HAS BEEN
01.17 T !"DIVIDED UP TO FIT SMALL COMPUTERS.
01.18 T !"EXPERIMENT IF YOU LIKE WITH G IN GROUP 1.
01.19 T !"CONSULT YOUR GUIDE SHEET FOR REENTRY POINTS.
01.20 T !"NOTE THAT THE COMPUTER TYPES * (ASTERISK) WHEN
01.21 T !"AWAITING COMMANDS.  IT TYPES A COLON : WHEN
01.22 T !"EXPECTING DATA OR RETURN."; Q
01.23 T !"LET'S LEARN ABOUT WRITE (OR W).  THIS COMMAND CAUSES A
01.24 T !"LINE TO BE WRITTEN OUT. FOR EXAMPLE:W 1.30. TRY IT"; Q
01.25 T !"NOTE THE STATEMENT NUMBER.  YOU DIDN'T SEE THIS WHEN
01.26 T !"THE PROGRAM WAS RUNNING.  IF YOU TYPE ONLY W, YOU WILL
01.27 T !"GET EVERYTHING.  USE CONTROL P TO HALT THIS.  IF YOU
01.28 T !"TYPE A DIGIT, YOU WILL GET EVERYTHING IN THAT GROUP.
01.29 T !"TRY W 1,W 1.20,W 1.23.  USE CONTROL P TO KEEP FROM
01.30 T !"GETTING A MILE OF PAPER.  IF YOU TRY TO WRITE
01.31 T !"A NON-EXISTENT STATEMENT, YOU JUST GET *";Q
01.32 T !"NEXT LET'S SEE HOW TO MAKE THE PROGRAM TYPE THINGS OUT."
01.33 T !"THE COMMAND IS TYPE (OR T).  TO JUST GET WRITING, YOU
01.34 T !"USE QUOTATION MARKS.  USE THE W COMMAND TO SEE ONE OF
01.35 T !"MY LINES AS AN EXAMPLE. "!"YOU CAN WRITE A PROGRAM
01.36 T !"OF YOUR OWN USING GROUP 5 WHICH I HAVE SAVED FOR YOU.
01.37 T !"TRY THE FOLLOWING :";W 5.01
01.38 T !" THE EXCLAMATION POINT IS A LINE FEED (ADVANCE PAPER)
01.39 T !"FOR THE TELETYPE. WHEN YOUR PROGRAM IS ENTERED
01.40 T !"IN GROUP 5, USE G 5.01 TO RUN IT.";Q
02.01 L I TEACH2
02.02 QUIT
05.01 T !"HELLO OUT THERE."
05.99 T !"CONSULT YOUR GUIDE SHEET FOR REENTRY POINT.";Q
*;G